From a9ccb2c2c8430fe9966211582dc411a323673b08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] xen/arm: guard vTPM device-model on GUEST_TPM_BASE (Xen 4.21)

Xen 4.21 dropped GUEST_TPM_BASE / GUEST_TPM_SIZE (the ARM vTPM guest
memory layout) from public/arch-arm.h. qemu 7.0.0's hw/arm/xen_arm.c
xen_enable_tpm() references GUEST_TPM_BASE inside an "#ifdef CONFIG_TPM"
block, so when CONFIG_TPM is enabled the build fails against 4.21 headers:

    hw/arm/xen_arm.c:368: error: 'GUEST_TPM_BASE' undeclared

vTPM is not used by this RPi5/Xen demo. Build the vTPM device-model
wiring only when BOTH CONFIG_TPM and the guest layout define are present,
so the same qemu source compiles against Xen 4.19 (define present) and
Xen 4.21 (define absent). On 4.21 vTPM is simply compiled out.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-4-8
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 hw/arm/xen_arm.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/arm/xen_arm.c b/hw/arm/xen_arm.c
--- a/hw/arm/xen_arm.c
+++ b/hw/arm/xen_arm.c
@@ -349,7 +349,10 @@ void qmp_xen_set_global_dirty_log(bool enable, Error **errp)

 static void xen_enable_tpm(void)
 {
-#ifdef CONFIG_TPM
+/* Xen 4.21 removed GUEST_TPM_BASE/GUEST_TPM_SIZE (ARM vTPM guest layout)
+ * from public/arch-arm.h. vTPM is unused in this demo; build the vTPM
+ * device-model wiring only when the guest layout define is present. */
+#if defined(CONFIG_TPM) && defined(GUEST_TPM_BASE)
     Error *errp = NULL;
     DeviceState *dev;
     SysBusDevice *busdev;
